From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 18:38:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 17/25] log streaming: redact validator values from external
 sinks

Argument and return validator failures include rejected values and validator details in their JsError messages. Replace those messages with fixed class-preserving text when serializing durable function-execution and exception events.

Apply the same protection to Sentry and PostHog Error Tracking, which build exception payloads outside the shared V1/V2 serializer. Preserve the existing full-display format for ordinary function-execution failures and the message-only format for ordinary exception sinks.

Add focused serialization and regression tests, and document the patch as an independently adoptable log-privacy unit.
